// Credential age alert: raise for review once a credential or signing key is
// 80 days old, ahead of a 90-day rotation policy. CREDENTIAL_AGE_DAYS is the
// age in whole days of the oldest credential in scope, published by the host.
// REGIME: all of them. Key age is a clock, not a market state.
// CONDITIONS: none, beyond the host knowing which credentials are in scope and
// what its own rotation limit is.
// INVALIDATION: rotation. Age returns to zero and the rule stops firing, with
// no memory of having fired - the host owns the ticket, not this rule.
// SHAPE: 1d; age changes once a day, and checking it faster only produces the
// same answer more often.
// NOT trusted_route_guard: that reports something already broken and proposes
// a pause. This one reports something that will break, so it proposes review
// and deliberately does not halt anything.
// CALIBRATED ON: a 90-day rotation policy, firing at 80 to leave ten days of
// warning. Neither number travels - both are policy figures, and a site with a
// 30-day policy should carry the same ten-day margin at 20.
strategy CredentialAgeAlert {

    agent SecurityDesk

    every 1d {

        if CREDENTIAL_AGE_DAYS >= 80 {

            observe()

        }

    }

}
